---
title: "Full Size"
description: "Stretches content across the full viewport width, for banners, headers or footers."
tags: [layout, utility, css]
usage: |
  Use a `<full-size>` element or the `full-size` class. It cancels the page's
  inline padding with negative margins, so it assumes the `1rem` inline padding
  set on `html` in the site's global styles. Combine it with a background color
  or image to make the section stand out.
accessibility: |
  - Check the contrast of text against the background you add.
  - If the section is a landmark, such as a site banner, use the matching element
    (`<header>`, `<footer>`) inside it.
---

<full-size>
  <style>
    @scope (full-size) {
      :scope {
        color: color-contrast(red);
        background-color: red;
      }
    }
  </style>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">
  <span>Look at me, i'm <strong>fully sized</strong>!</span>
</full-size>
